### WhatsApp API Requests

@base_url = http://localhost:5001

### Health Check
GET {{base_url}}/
Content-Type: application/json

### Send Text Message
POST {{base_url}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "cellphone": "5511999999999",
    "message": "Hello! This is a test message from the Redis Queue system. 🚀",
    "type": "text"
}

### Send Image Message (with Base64)
# Replace media_data with actual base64 string
POST {{base_url}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "cellphone": "5511999999999",
    "message": "Check out this image!",
    "type": "image",
    "media_data": "iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mP8z8BQDwAEhQGAhKmMIQAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==",
    "media_mime_type": "image/png",
    "media_filename": "test.png"
}

### Send Document
POST {{base_url}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "cellphone": "5511999999999",
    "message": "Here is the documentation you requested.",
    "type": "document",
    "media_data": "UEsDBBQAAAAIA...", 
    "media_mime_type": "application/pdf",
    "media_filename": "report.pdf"
}

### Simulate Incoming WhatsApp Message (Internal API)
# This is what the Node.js worker calls when it receives a message
POST {{base_url}}/incoming-whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "from": "5511999999999@c.us",
    "body": "Hi there! I'm responding to your test.",
    "type": "text",
    "timestamp": 1678234567
}
